---
title: Grants
---
body:

About our grants program
-------------------------

Apply now: https://forms.gle/z27de5EiKZZ3kN8U7

**Deadline: December 19, 2020** (`AoE <https://www.worldtimeserver.com/time-zones/aoe/>`__)

Our grants program is an important tool that helps us realize a goal of creating
an inclusive, respectful conference that welcomes people of all races, ethnicities,
genders, ages, abilities, religions, and sexual orientations. We provide financial
assistance so people who might otherwise not be able to afford to join our event can.

Attendees who receive grants will have the cost of their ticket paid for by
PyCascades. Speakers who receive grants can have some or all of the cost of
the audio & video equipment needed to present at our virtual conference covered.

We actively encourage people to apply for these grants. Just as in the previous
three years, we are dedicating a large portion of our budget to grants.

Our grants program prioritizes people with relatively low income, speakers,
active builders of Python community, and notable open source contributors.
However, anyone who would be financially burdened by attending PyCascades
is welcome to apply.